From 2c741a9578b13a90f4201e4f5ad7940f561e515b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin Stark <gavin@gstark.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:24:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [network] Add status code filters to the Network panel

Add a filter group with 2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx and Custom... buttons after
the resource type filters. The status class buttons work like the
resource type buttons: a click selects one class, and Ctrl+click (Cmd+click
on Mac) selects more than one.

Custom... opens an input for a status code expression: single codes
(404), ranges (200-204 or 200..204), comparisons (>=500, !=304) and
comma-separated lists of these. A request matches if it matches any
selected class or the expression. While the expression is empty, the
Custom button does not filter. Requests with status code 0 never match.

Bug: none
